{
  "id": "a2-rational-notes",
  "version": 1,
  "title": "Rational functions and sequences: cheat sheet",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "b1",
      "kind": "text",
      "title": "The big idea",
      "body": "Rational expressions are fractions of polynomials. Sequences list numbers with a pattern, and series add them. Probability and the normal curve measure chance and spread."
    },
    {
      "id": "b2",
      "kind": "list",
      "title": "Rational expressions",
      "items": [
        "Factor, then cancel common factors",
        "Never allow a zero denominator",
        "Add using a common denominator",
        "Check solutions: reject extraneous ones"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b3",
      "kind": "formula",
      "title": "Arithmetic sequence",
      "body": "$a_n=a_1+(n-1)d$"
    },
    {
      "id": "b4",
      "kind": "formula",
      "title": "Geometric sequence",
      "body": "$a_n=a_1\\cdot r^{n-1}$"
    },
    {
      "id": "b5",
      "kind": "formula",
      "title": "Arithmetic series",
      "body": "$S_n=\\frac{n(a_1+a_n)}{2}$"
    },
    {
      "id": "b6",
      "kind": "formula",
      "title": "Geometric series",
      "body": "$S_n=\\frac{a_1(1-r^n)}{1-r}$, and $\\frac{a_1}{1-r}$ if $|r|<1$"
    },
    {
      "id": "b7",
      "kind": "list",
      "title": "Probability and the normal curve",
      "items": [
        "$P=\\frac{\\text{favourable}}{\\text{total}}$, between 0 and 1",
        "Independent: $P(A\\text{ and }B)=P(A)P(B)$",
        "68%, 95%, 99.7% within 1, 2, 3 $\\sigma$",
        "$z=\\frac{x-\\mu}{\\sigma}$"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b8",
      "kind": "tip",
      "body": "Complement trick: for 'at least one', compute $1-P(\\text{none})$."
    }
  ]
}